.TH JOBWRAPD 8 "August 2026" "jobwrap 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
jobwrapd \- the per-user jobwrap daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jobwrapd
[\fB--foreground\fR] [\fB--socket \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBjobwrapd\fR is the per-user daemon that provides the web interface, HTTP
API, authentication, job registry, log storage, and access control for
jobwrap. It runs as the invoking user, never as root, and never creates
arbitrary processes.
.PP
It is normally started automatically by \fBjobwrap\fR, or through the user
systemd units. It binds an HTTP listener to loopback and listens on a private
Unix socket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground and do not detach.
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Path to the Unix socket (defaults to the XDG runtime dir).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/jobwrap/daemon.sock
The private socket (mode 0600).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/jobwrap/daemon.pid
The daemon pid.
.SH SECURITY
The daemon verifies each socket peer's UID via SO_PEERCRED. The HTTP server
binds to loopback by default. Configuration and the security model are
documented in jobwrap(1) and the installed README.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jobwrap (1),
.BR jobwrap.toml (5)
